                    owl:intersectionOf ( ns1:IAO_0000101 ns1:OBI_0001305 ) ] ],
        ns1:OBI_0000435 .

ns1:OBI_0302743 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete_liver"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "liver"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 2104732. Caudate lobe of the liver: anatomy, embryology, and pathology.\\nAJR Am J Roentgenol. 1990 Jan;154(1):87-93."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000125 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "liver is an anatomical entity which constituent are mainly hepatocytes, which has a function of detoxification, hematopoietic center, glucose and fat metabolism management. liver is only found in animals , all Vertebrates and some families of invertebrates"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial Branch"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000231 ns1:IAO_0000228 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000232 "PRS: Test. added for evaluation and validation of possible imports from CARO (or other anatomical resources)"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass> ;
    owl:deprecated true .

ns1:OBI_0302745 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete_adipose tissue"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "adipose tissue"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18435934.Fatty acid composition of adipose tissue and blood in humans and its use as a biomarker of dietary intake.Prog Lipid Res. 2008 Apr 4."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000125 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "adipose tissue is a tissue which main constituents are adipocytes. adipose tissue can be classified base on its location (site) but also based on adipocyte subtypes (brown or white) which reflect functional differences and is only found in animals, Vertebrates or invertebrates."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial derived"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000231 ns1:IAO_0000228 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000232 "PRS: this class has been added during major biomaterial.owl cleanup for evaluation and testing of imports from CARO"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass> ;
    owl:deprecated true .

ns1:OBI_0302835 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "denatured polymer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "denatured polymer"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Is a polymer which has lost secondary or tertiary structure"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denaturation_%28biochemistry%29"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:CHEBI_33839,
        ns1:OBI_0000047 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( ns1:CHEBI_33839 [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000803 ] ) ] .

ns1:OBI_0302837 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "decapitated organism"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "decapitated organism"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Ovarian development induced in decapitated female Culex pipiens pallens mosquitoes by infusion of physiological quantities of 20-hydroxyecdysone together with amino acids.\\nJ Insect Physiol. 1998 May;44(5-6):525-528. PMID: 12770172"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "decapitated organism is an organism which has had it's head removed"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI Biomaterial"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000047 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( ns1:BFO_0000040 [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0302899 ] ) ] .

ns1:OBI_0302838 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "validated information"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "validated information"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 20084519: \"..Three of four interactions were validated via functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) in an independent sample of healthy controls;...\""^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "an information content entity which results from a validation process aimed at confirming a claim, a finding or a predicted information entity about a material entity or a process by experimental means."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0302911 ],
        ns1:IAO_0000030 .

ns1:OBI_0302840 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "curated information"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "curated information"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 17344875: A curated compendium of phosphorylation motifs.Nat Biotechnol. 2007 Mar;25(3):285-6."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A information content entity that has undergone a digital curation performed by a curator for accuracy checks and compliance with curation requirements. Information which has been assessed for accuracy by domain experts."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "2009-11-10 Bjoern Peters. Need to check if this was intended. overlap with 'edited information', and has the same logical restrictions."^^xsd:string,
        "2010-01-31 Philippe Rocca-Serra: restriction now changed to be the output of a digital curation process + reflected in example of usage and reference"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:Bjoern Peters"^^xsd:string,
        "Person:Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0302914 ],
        ns1:IAO_0000030 .

ns1:OBI_0302846 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "randomized group participant role"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "randomized group participant role"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "A person enrolled in a randomized clinical trial bears a randomized group participant role"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a role that borne by an organism and realized by some group randomization process"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson"^^xsd:string,
        "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:BFO_0000023 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0302900 ] .

ns1:OBI_0302847 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "methylated polymer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "methylated polymer"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Binding and penetration of methylated DNA into primary and transformed human cells.\\nAnn N Y Acad Sci. 2008 Aug;1137:36-40. PMID: 18837922"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A methylated polymer which has artificially acquired one or more methyl groups"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI Biomaterial"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:CHEBI_33839,
        ns1:OBI_0000047 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( ns1:CHEBI_33839 [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0600039 ] ) ] .

ns1:OBI_0302867 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "predicted data item"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "predicted data item"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A data item that was generated on the basis of a calculation or logical reasoning"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "BP 12/21: Edited the incomplete definition from Philippe. It is still unclear to me if this should be a data item at all, or an information content entity. This will be important, because if we exclude predictions from data items, we will run into issues that we willl have to duplicate things like 'weight datum' etc. all of which can be predicted. "^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra; Bjoern Peters"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:IAO_0000027 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0302910 ] .

ns1:OBI_0302868 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mean-centered data"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "mean-centered data"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a data item which has been processed by a mean centering data transformation where each output value is produced by subtracting the mean from the inout value"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson"^^xsd:string,
        "Person:Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000451 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0200029 ] .

ns1:OBI_0302876 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dissolved material entity"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "dissolved material entity"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Salt molecules that have been mixed into water"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A material entity that has been going through a process of being put into solution"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:Bjoern Peters"^^xsd:string,
        "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000576 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( ns1:BFO_0000040 ns1:OBI_0000576 [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000050 ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom [ a owl:Restriction ;
                                owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
                                owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000685 ] ] ) ] .

ns1:OBI_0302888 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "washing"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "washing"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 6874122. Dialysis leucopenia--no correction after prolonged washing of the membrane. Int J Artif Organs. 1983 May;6(3):113-4."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "washing is a process by which a material entity acting as  contaminant (e.g. excess staining reagent) is removed by application of one or more cycles of solution in flow."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI-Branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000299 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:BFO_0000040 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000417 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000456 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000293 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:BFO_0000040 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000094 .

ns1:OBI_0302889 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "irradiation"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "irradiation"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18563778.Histological and modeling study of skin thermal injury to 2.0 mum laser irradiation.Lasers Surg Med. 2008 Jun 18;40(5):358-370."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "irradiation is a process by which a material entity is exposed to radiative energy, which could be ionizing radiation (such as gamma rays or X-rays)  or not such as UV light or microwaves"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "adapted from wikipedia (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irradiation)"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000057 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400065 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000293 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:BFO_0000040 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000417 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000456 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000094 .

ns1:OBI_0302891 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "trypsination"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "trypsination"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "The use of mild trypsinization conditions in the detachment of endothelial cells to promote subsequent endothelialization on synthetic surfaces. Biomaterials. 2007 Sep;28(27):3928-35. PMID: 17570483"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000125 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "trypsination is a protease cleavage which uses enzyme trypsin to act on proteins present in an input material entity"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI PA"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0600056 .

ns1:OBI_0302895 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "electrocution"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "electrocution"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 9587208. Electrocution of horses and cattle. Vet Rec. 1998 Apr 4;142(14):376."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "electrocution is process by which electric current is applied to a material with quality alive and result the termination of life process."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000057 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400142 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000919 .

ns1:OBI_0302896 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cervical dislocation"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "cervical dislocation"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18246869. Loss of cortical function in mice after decapitation, cervical dislocation, potassium chloride injection, and CO2 inhalation. Comp Med. 2007 Dec;57(6):570-3"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "cervical dislocation is a process by which a Vertebrate organism has its life terminated by rupturing spinal cord between cervical vertebrae induced by excessive mechanical torsion"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "PRS:21102008: Input must be restricted to Vertebrates (requires import from NCBI tax)"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000919 .

ns1:OBI_0302897 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "asphyxiation"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "asphyxiation"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18246869. Loss of cortical function in mice after decapitation, cervical dislocation, potassium chloride injection, and CO2 inhalation. Comp Med. 2007 Dec;57(6):570-"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "asphyxiation is a process by which oxygen supplies are restricted (by mechanical, e.g obstructing airways or chemical means, e.g. increasing CO2 partial pressure) resulting in termination of life in oxygen reliant organisms."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000919 .

ns1:OBI_0302898 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "intentional overdosing"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "intentional overdosing"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "In vivo measurement of tumor blood oxygenation by near-infrared spectroscopy: immediate effects of pentobarbital overdose or carmustine treatment.\\nJ Neurooncol. 1994;22(3):209-20. PMID: 7760097"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "intentional overdosing is a process by which an excess dose of a chemical compound is given with the intent of causing death"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "lethal injection"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI Biomaterial"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000293 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:CHEBI_23367 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000919 .

ns1:OBI_0302901 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete_activation"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "activation"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18566411.Activation of the JAK/STAT-1 Signaling Pathway by IFN-{gamma} Can Down-Regulate Functional Expression of the MHC Class I-Related Neonatal Fc Receptor for IgG.J Immunol. 2008 Jul 1;181(1):449-63."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000124 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a process by which a material entity status is modified and conferred a capability of reacting\\n(this sounds like a circular definition , hugh!)"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "Alan Ruttenberg 2010/11/22: After OBI call, this is too broad a term, and in any case would be in the scope of GO"^^xsd:string,
        "See tracker:\\nhttps://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?func=detail&aid=3302925&group_id=177891&atid=886178"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI-Branch"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000231 ns1:IAO_0000103 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass> ;
    owl:deprecated true .

ns1:OBI_0302902 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "immobilization"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "immobilization"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18562258. The immobilization of proteins on biodegradable fibers via biotin-streptavidin bridges.Acta Biomater. 2008 May 23."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "immbolization is a process by which material entity become (possibly covalently but not necessarily) attached to the surface of another material entity used a substratum."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI-Branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000417 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000456 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000094 .

ns1:OBI_0302906 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "DNA Subtraction"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "DNA Subtraction"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 10718422. Identification of genes overexpressed in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma using a combination of complementary DNA subtraction and microarray analysis. Laryngoscope. 2000 Mar;110(3 Pt 1):374-81"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a material separation process by which repetitive genomic DNA is removed during the construction of cDNA library."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI-Branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000417 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000681 ],
        ns1:OBI_0600014 .

ns1:OBI_0302912 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "electroporation"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "electroporation"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18551712. Microfluidic electroporation for selective release of intracellular molecules at the single-cell level. Electrophoresis. 2008 Jun 13."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a process in which a significant increase in the electrical conductivity and permeability of the cell plasma membrane caused by an externally applied electrical field. It is usually used in molecular biology as a way of introducing some substance into a cell, such as loading it with a molecular probe, a drug that can change the cell's function, or a piece of coding DNA"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "electropermeabilization"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "WEB:http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electroporation"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000293 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:CL_0000000 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000057 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400142 ],
        ns1:OBI_0600033 .

ns1:OBI_0400005 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "A10-Analyzer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "A10-Analyzer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A A10 is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Apogee. It uses an arc lamp as a light source, with choices of 75W Xe, 75W Xe/Hg or 100W Hg arc lamps. It has filters and collectors for up to three fluorescent parameters and two scatter parameters. It uses analog electronics. The A10 can be used for measuring the properties of individual cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.apogeeflow.com/flow_cytometry_products.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400006 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "A40-MiniFCM"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "A40-MiniFCM"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A A40-MiniFCM is a flow_cytometer_analyser that allows for the choice of one of four lasers (375nm, 405nm,488nm, 532nm, 635nm), and PMTs and filters for collecting up to four parameters. It uses digital electronics. A military version of this cytometer is available as well. The A40-MiniFCM is geared towards the most demanding applications such as archaea, bacteria and large virus."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.apogeeflow.com/flow_cytometry_products.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400007 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "analog-to-digital converter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "analog-to-digital converter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "The analog to digital converter transformed the analog output from the photomultiplier tube to a digital signal for collection."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "An analog-to-digital_converter is an instrument that converts an infinite resolution analog signal to a finite resolution digital signal."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en,
        "Melanie Courtot"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "A-D"@en,
        "A2D"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Analog-to-Digital_Converter"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000393 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0400009 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "arc lamp"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "arc lamp"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "The Jablochkoff Candle"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Arc lamp is a light source that produces light by an electric arc (or voltaic arc). The lamp consists of two electrodes typically made of tungsten which are separated by a gas. The type of lamp is often named by the gas contained in the bulb; including neon, argon, xenon, krypton, sodium, metal halide, and mercury. The electric arc in an arc lamp consists of gas which is initially ionized by a voltage and is therefore electrically conductive. To start an arc lamp, usually a very high voltage is needed to ignite or strike the arc. This requires an electrical circuit sometimes called an igniter, which is part of a larger circuit called the ballast. The ballast supplies a suitable voltage and current to the lamp as its electrical characteristics change with temperature and time. Older cytometers may use arc lamps to irradiate particles at the interrogation point."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arc_lamp"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400065 .

ns1:OBI_0400010 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "argon ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "argon ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "argon ion laser in a cytometer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "An argon-ion laser is an ion laser that uses argon ions as the lasing medium. These lasers are used primarily to emit light at wave lengths of 458 nm, 488 nm or 514.5 nm, though it is possible to use them to emit several wavelengths of blue and green light. Argon-ion lasers can emit light at many different wave lenghts, and excite a number of different flourochromes."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser#Gas_lasers"^^xsd:string,
        "John Quinn"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400060 .

ns1:OBI_0400011 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "avalanche photodiode"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "avalanche photodiode"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "C30644E -  InGaAs Avalanche Photodiode"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "An avalanche photodiode is typically used to collect photons emitted by forward scatter because it is far less sensitive, and less likely o be burned out, than a PMT. A photodiode with high quantum efficiency and a mechanism for producing gains as high as a few thousand."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400083 .

ns1:OBI_0400012 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Bactiflow"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Bactiflow"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Bactiflow is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Chemunex SA. It is a cell counter for bacteria and other micro organisms. Bacteria are stained with a fluorochrome and the number of particles that fluoresce are counted. The system uses digital electronics, a single laser and a single detector. An ALS version is available as well - Automatic Labeling System. The Bactiflow is specialized cytometer used exclusively for counting microbes."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.chemunex.com/products/chemframe.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400013 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "band pass filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "band pass filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "530/30 BP filter, 585/42 BP filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A band pass filter is an optical filter that passes wavelengths of light within a certain range and rejects (attenuates) frequencies outside that range. The passed wavelengths are indicated in the specifications of the filter and its name. A 480/20 band-pass filter pass light with at wavelengths of 460 to 500 nm and attenuates all others."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Band_pass_filter"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400079 .

ns1:OBI_0400014 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BioSorter1000"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "BioSorter1000"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "BioSorter 1000 at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A BioSorter1000 is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Union Biometrica. It includes analog electronics, 488/514 nm multi-line Argon-ion laser for fluorescence and a light stabilized 670 nm forward scatter laser for extinction and time-of-flight. It has filters and PMTs for 3 fluorescent parameters and photodiodes for scatter, time of flight, and extinction. The flow cell is quartz cuvette. The BioSorterTM 1000 is an instrument for analyzing and sorting objects from 200-600 microns in diameter."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.unionbio.com/products/BioSorter.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400015 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BioSorter2000"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "BioSorter2000"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "BioSorter 2000 at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A BioSorter2000 is a sorter manufactured by Union Biometrica. It includes analog electronics, 488/514 nm multi-line Argon-ion laser for fluorescence and a light stabilized 670 nm forward scatter laser for extinction and time-of-flight. It has filters and PMTs for 3 fluorescent parameters and photodiodes for scatter, time of flight, and extinction. The flow cell is quartz cuvette. The BioSorterTM 2000 is an instrument for analyzing and sorting objects from 500 microns to 1.5 millimeters in diameter."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.unionbio.com/products/BioSorter.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400016 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BioSorter250"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "BioSorter250"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "BioSorter 250 at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A BioSorter250 is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Union Biometrica. It includes analog electronics, 488/514 nm multi-line Argon-ion laser for fluorescence and a light stabilized 670 nm forward scatter laser for extinction and time-of-flight. It has filters and PMTs for 3 fluorescent parameters and photodiodes for scatter, time of flight, and extinction. The flow cell is quartz cuvette. The BioSorterTM 250 is an instrument for analyzing and sorting objects from 40-200 microns in diameter."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.unionbio.com/products/BioSorter.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400017 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BioSorter500"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "BioSorter500"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "BioSorter 500 at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A BioSorter500 is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Union Biometrica. It includes analog electronics, 488/514 nm multi-line Argon-ion laser for fluorescence and a light stabilized 670 nm forward scatter laser for extinction and time-of-flight. It has filters and PMTs for 3 fluorescent parameters and photodiodes for scatter, time of flight, and extinction. The flow cell is quartz cuvette. The BioSorterTM 500 is an instrument for analyzing and sorting objects from 100-250 microns in diameter and less than 2mm in length."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.unionbio.com/products/BioSorter.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400018 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cell Lab Quanta SC"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Cell Lab Quanta SC"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Cell Lab Quanta SC is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Becman Coulter. It features a mercury arc lamp optimized at 366, 405, and 435 nm, and a 488 nm laser diode. It has filters and PMTs to collect up to 3 fluorescent parameters, and a photodiode for side scatter detection. This cytometer uses Couter-Volume for cell size measurements. The Cell Lab Quanta SC can be used for measuring the properties of individual cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.beckmancoulter.com/cell-lab"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400019 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "charge plate"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "charge plate"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 charge plate"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics subsystem. Charge plates are used or sorters. They create an charged electric field when particles deemed to be desired for further analysis are shaken form the piexo electric crystal. The charged particles are drawn toward the charged plate, and the altered drop location causes the particles to fall into a collection tube. Charge plates enable sorting."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000374 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000383 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0400020 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cell sorter collection tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "cell sorter collection tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 collection tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics subsystem. The collection tube is a vessel for capturing cells of interest that have been identified by a sorter. The collection tube is the end location of sorted cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000836 .

ns1:OBI_0400022 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cyan"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Cyan"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Cyan is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Dako Cytomation. It features include digital electronics, three lasers: 488 nm, 635 nm, and 405 nm, and filters and collectors for nine fluorescent parameters and two scatter parameters. The Cyan can be used for measuring the properties of individual cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.dakousa.com/prod_productrelatedinformation?url=gprod_cyan_index.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400023 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CYFlow ML"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CYFlow ML"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A CyFlow_ML is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Partec. It is a digital machine which uses 4 light sources: triple laser configurations including new powerful 200mW@488nm blue solid state laser + 100W UV lamp for highest resolution DNA analysis, and can collect 16 optical parameters: FSC1, FSC2, SSC, FL1-FL13. Ultracompact high end desktop multilaser Flow Cytometer for all applications in cell analysis and absolute counting."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.partec.de/products/cyflow-ml.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400024 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CyFlow SL"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CyFlow SL"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Partec. Its specs are: ultracompact and fully equipped mobile/portable instrument, dimensions [cm]: L 43 x H 16 x D 37, highest stability/robustness and highest precision, 5 optical parameters: FSC, SSC, FL-1, FL-2, FL-3, 20mW@488nm blue solid state laser , other laser light sources optional (UV, violet, green, red), WindowsTM XP FloMax (software for real time data acquisition, data display, and data evaluation), parallel 16 bit digital pulse processing Compact mobile Flow Cytometer for any kind of cell analysis and absolute volumetric counting. The CyFlow_SL allows to analyze forward and side scatter signals in combination with up to 3 fluorescence channels."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.partec.de/products/cyflow.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400025 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CyFlow SL3"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CyFlow SL3"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A CyFlow_Sl3 is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Partec. Its specs are: ultracompact and fully equipped mobile/portable instrument, dimensions [cm]: L 43 x H 16 x D 37 , highest stability/robustness and highest precision, 5 optical parameters: FSC, SSC, FL-1, FL-2, FL-3, 20mW@488nm blue solid state laser, other laser light sources optional (UV, violet, green, red), WindowsTM XP FloMax (software for real time data acquisition, data display, and data evaluation), parallel 16 bit digital pulse processing. The CyFlow SL3 is a compact and dedicated portable Flow Cytometer for accurate and affordable cell analysis and true volumetric absolute counting in HIV Monitoring and AIDS patient follow-up by precise and direct CD4 and CD4% measurement."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.partec.de/products/cyflowsl3.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400026 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CyFlow Space"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CyFlow Space"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "CyFlow Space at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A CyFlow_Space is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Partec. Its specs are: 8optical parameters, 6 colours:FSC, SSC, FL1-FL6 , 3laser light sources: 200mW@488nm blue solid state laser 25mW@635nm red diode laser 50mW@405nm violet or 8mW@375nm ultraviolet diode laser _ultracompact desktop high end instrument. Parallel 16bit digital pulse processing. The CyFlow Space is a 6-Colour FCM System and Cell Sorter for Clinical Routine and Research."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.partec.de/products/cyflowspace.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400027 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CytoBuoy flow cytometer analyzer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CytoBuoy"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "CytoBuoy can be used to conduct extended and/or high frequency time series of phytoplankton distribution and abundance on fixed locations"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A flow cytometer analyser which is manufactured by Cyto Buoy Inc. They are the buoy mounted version of the CytoSense, equipped with wireless transmission of control and data files. They are a single laser, multi parameter instrument. Various types of micro-laser are offered; available measuring parameters are forward light scatter, side scatter, and fluorescence (max. 9 colour bands). The current series have 5 parameters."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn, Melanie Courtot"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.cytobuoy.com/"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:hasValue ns1:OBI_0001458 ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000304 ],
        ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400028 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CytoSence"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CytoSence"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A CytoSense is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Cyto Buoy Inc. They are a single laser, multi parameter instrument. Various types of micro-laser are offered; available measuring parameters are forward light scatter, side scatter, and fluorescence (max. 9 colour bands). The current series have 5 parameters. The CytoSense is the basic instrument, which can be used for normal laboratory applications, as well as for autonomous monitoring with internal data logging or direct data transmission. The special instrument design and its splashproof housing allow operation on moving platforms and outdoor sites."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.cytobuoy.com/"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400029 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CytoSub"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "CytoSub"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A CytoSub is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Cyto Buoy Inc. They are a single laser, multi parameter instrument. Various types of micro-laser are offered; available measuring parameters are forward light scatter, side scatter, and fluorescence (max. 9 colour bands). The current series have 5 parameters. The CytoSub is the submersible version equipped with a high pressure sample inlet loop and a high pressure housing to allow underwater operation down to 200 m, lowered on a cable or mounted on a flooded underwater vehicle."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.cytobuoy.com/"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400030 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dichroic filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "dichroic filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Cy3 Dichroic Filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A dichroic filter is an optical filter which is used to selectively pass light of a small range of colors while reflecting other colors. A dichroic filter passes the specified range of light whereas a dichroic mirror reflects the specified range of light."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dichroic_filter"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400079 .

ns1:OBI_0400031 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dichroic mirror"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "dichroic mirror"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "ViewLux Alexa 594 dichroic mirror"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A dichroic mirror is an optical filter which is used to selectively reflect light of a small range of colors while passing other colors. A dichroic filter passes the specified range of light whereas a dichroic mirror reflects the specified range of light."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dichroic_mirror"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400079 .

ns1:OBI_0400032 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "differential pressure gauge"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "differential pressure gauge"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 differential pressure gauge"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics subsystem. The differential pressure gauge monitors the difference between sample and sheath fluid pressures in systems where pressure is used to force the sample fluid to flow in the center of the sheath fluid. A differential pressure gauge can be used by the operator to make sure that the sample fluid is at a greater pressure than the sheath fluid, which maintains a core of sample fluid."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000453 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000832 .

ns1:OBI_0400033 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "diode laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "diode laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "FAX-RS3-H0 diode laser manufactured by Diode Laser Concepts, Inc."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A diode laser is a laser in which the active medium is a p-n junction semiconductor laser diode, similar to that found in a light-emitting diode. Laser diodes emit at wavelengths from 375 nm to 1800 nm, and wavelengths of over 3 micrometer have been demonstrated. A diode laser can by used to irradiate cells in a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "John Quinn"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400064 .

ns1:OBI_0400034 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dye laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "dye laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Rhodamine 101 dye laser used to irradiate cells in a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A dye laser is a laser in which the lasing medium is a fluorescent dye, usually dissolved in an organic solvent such as ethanol or ethylene glycol. The particular dye used determines the wavelengths the laser can emit. The laser medium is places between two parallel mirrors for light emission amplification."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "John Quinn"@en,
        "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400064 .

ns1:OBI_0400036 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FACS Calibur"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FACS Calibur"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "\"FACS Calibur at TFL, BCCRC, Vancouver\""@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The FACS Calibur is one of the most popular cytometers in use for research."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "\"http://www.bdbiosciences.com/immunocytometry_systems/products/display_product.php?keyID=45, 2007-05-11\""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400037 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FACS Canto"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FACS Canto"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A FACS_Canto is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Becton Dickinson. It features digital electronics, a solid state 488 nm, and a HeNe 633 nm lasers, and filters and PMTs for collecting up to 6 fluorescent parameters. The FACS_Canto is an analyser usually used in clinical applications."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.bdbiosciences.com/pdfs/brochures/23-8742-00.pdf"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400038 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FACS Canto2"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FACS Canto2"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A FACS_Canto2 is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by BD. It features digital electronics, two solid state lasers at 488 and 633 nm with the option for a third 405 nm laser, and filters and collectors for measuring up to 8 fluorescent paramters with either the 2 or 3 laser option. The FACS_Canto2 is an analyser usually used in clinical applications."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.bdbiosciences.com/cgi-bin/literature/view?part_num=23-8786-01"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400039 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FACS Scan"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FACS Scan"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A FACS_Scan is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Becton Dickinson. IT features analog electronics, one 488 nm solid state laser, and the filters and PMTs to collect up to three fluorescent parameters The FACS_Scan is usually used for research applications."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.brc.ubc.ca/brc/facs.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400040 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FACSAria"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FACSAria"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "FACSAria at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A FASCSAria is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Becton Dickinson. It features digital electronics, a solid state 488 nm blue laser, a solid state 407 nm violet laser, and a HeNe (633 nm) ion laser. The Aria has the filters and PMTs to collect side scatter and 9 fluorescent parameters. The Aria has a photodiode detector for forward scatter collector. The flow cell is Quartz cuvette. The FACSAria is a sorter used to collect and analyse cells using up to 11 parameters."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.bdbiosciences.com/external_files/is/doc/mkt_lit/brochures/SJ-0003-00Aria.pdf"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400041 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FACSvantage"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FACSvantage"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "FACSvantage at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The FACSvantage is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Becton Dickinson. It has analog electronics, three lasers (several options are available), and the filters and PMTs to collect 6 fluorescent parameters and side scatter, and a photodiode to collect forward scatter. The FACSvantage can be used to analyse, sort and collect cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.bdbiosciences.com/features/products/display_product.php?keyID=42"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400042 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "FC 500"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "FC 500"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A FC_500 is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Beckman Coulter. It features digital electronics, 488 nm and 635 nm lasers, filters and PMTs for 5 fluorescent parameters, a diode for collecting side scatter and a solid state detector for forward scatter. The FC 500 is an analyser usually used for either research or clinical applications."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.beckmancoulter.com/products/instrument/flowcytometry/fc500series.asp"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400045 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fluid pressure regulator"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "fluid pressure regulator"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 fluid pressure regulator"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidic subsystem. The fluid pressure regulator maintains constant pressure within the sheath and or sample lines by filling the lines with enough gas to push the fluid at the desired rate. The gas is usually air, and less frequently nitrogen. In the sheath line, the gas is pushed into the sheath tank. In the sample line the gas is pushed into the collection tube. Fluid pressure regulators maintain great enough pressure to push sample fluid out of the tube and sheath fluid out of the sheath tank."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person: John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000453 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000401 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000832,
        ns1:OBI_0002089 .

ns1:OBI_0400048 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guava EasyCyte Mini"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Guava EasyCyte Mini"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Guava_EasyCyte_Mini is a flow_cytometer_analyser that includes a single 488 nm laser, and filters and PMTs to collect up to 3 fluorescent parameters. It includes a photodiode forward scatter collector and an optional photodiode for side scatter collection.Guava cytometers use aspiration instead of fluid systems to transport cells within the machine. The mini accepts tubes only for inputting cells or beads. The Guava_EasyCyte_Mini cytometer is a small portable cytometer particularly useful for field measurement."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.guavatechnologies.com/main/products/easyCyteMini.cfm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400049 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guava EasyCyte Plus"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Guava EasyCyte Plus"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Guava_EasyCyte_Plus System is a flow_cytometer_analyser that includes a single 488 nm laser, and filters and PMTs to collect up to 4 fluorescent parameters. It includes a photodiode forward scatter collector and an optional photodiode for side scatter collection.Guava cytometers use aspiration instead of fluid systems to transport cells within the machine. The EasyCyte plus accepts 96 well plates as well as tubes. The Guava_EasyCyte_Plus cytometer is a small portable cytometer particularly useful for field measurement."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.guavatechnologies.com/main/products/easycyte-new.cfm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400050 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guava Personal Cell Analysis"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Guava Personal Cell Analysis"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A  Guava_Personal_Cell_Analysis System is a flow_cytometer_analyser that includes a single 532 nm laser, and filters and PMTs to collect up to 2 fluorescent parameters. It includes a photodiode forward scatter collector. Guava cytometers use aspiration instead of fluid systems to transport cells within the machine. The PCA96 uses only tubes to introduce specimen. The Guava PCA cytometer is a small portable cytometer particularly useful for field measurement."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "Guava_PCA"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.guavatechnologies.com/main/products/PCA-new.cfm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400051 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guava Personal Cell Analysis-96"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Guava Personal Cell Analysis-96"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The Guava_Personal_Cell_Analysis-96 Systems is a flow_cytometer_analyser that includes a single 532 nm laser, and filters and PMTs to collect up to 2 fluorescent parameters. It includes a photodiode forward scatter collector. Guava cytometers use aspiration instead of fluid systems to transport cells within the machine. The PCA96 uses either tubes or 96 well plates to introduce specimen. The Guava PCA -96 cytometer is a small portable cytometer particularly useful for field measurement."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "Guava_PCA-96"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.guavatechnologies.com/main/products/PCA-96new.cfm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400052 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "helium cadmium ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "helium cadmium ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "KIMMON HeCd 325nm laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A helium-cadmium laser is a metal vapor laser that emits wavelengths of 442, 325 and 354 nms. This laser is a metal vapor laser. A helium-cadmium laser can by used to irradiate cells in a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser#Gas_lasers"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400073 .

ns1:OBI_0400053 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "helium neon ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "helium neon ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "A helium neon laser can by used to irradiate cells in a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A helium-neon laser (HeNe) is an ion laser that uses helium and neon gas-ions as lasing medium. HeNe lasers emit at 543 nm and 633 nm most commonly and can also be used at 543, 594, and 611 nm."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser#Gas_lasers"^^xsd:string,
        "John Quinn"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400060 .

ns1:OBI_0400054 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Amnis ImageStream"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Amnis ImageStream"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The ImageStream is a multispectral_imaging_flow_cytometer manufactured by Amnis. Its has digital electronics, a single standard 488 nm solid state laser. In addition an optional 658 nm and your choice of either a 405 nm or 375 nm solid state laser can be added. Information is collected using cameras. The ImageStream system CCD camera produces six images of each cell, including darkfield, brightfield, and up to four fluorescent colors. Each image is used to calculate over 40 features, so a six-image assay results in ~250 morphometric and photometric features per cell. The ImageStream is a flow cytometer that takes pictures of the cells in flow.\\nIt has both components, an Image cytometer and a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "It has both components, an Image cytometer and a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en,
        "Melanie Courtot"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.amnis.com/"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000051 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400135 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000051 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400044 ],
        ns1:OBI_0400146 .

ns1:OBI_0400055 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "inFlux Analyzer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "inFlux Analyzer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The inFlux Analyzer is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Cytopeia. It is a digital machine, with these laser options: Coherent 70, 90, 300 series water cooled lasers, solid state UV 355nm, Violet 408nm, Violet-Blue 479nm, Blue-488nm, Green-531nm, Red-635nm, Red-647nm. Filters and PMTs are used for all parameters (including forward light scatter), and up to 12 PMTs can be included. The Influx analyser can be used to measure the properties of individual cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.cytopeia.com/analyzer.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400056 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Influx Cell Sorter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Influx Cell Sorter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Influx Cell Sorter at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Influx Cell Sorter is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Cytopeia. It is a digital machine, with these laser options: Coherent 70, 90, 300 series water cooled lasers, solid state UV 355nm, Violet 408nm, Violet-Blue 479nm, Blue-488nm, Green-531nm, Red-635nm, Red-647nm. The sorting is multi-way, index, and proportional sorting. Filters and PMTs are used for all parameters (including forward light scatter), and up to 12 PMTs can be included. The Influx cell sorter can be used to measure, sort, and collect ndividual cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.cytopeia.com/sorter.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400059 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "interrogation_point"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "interrogation_point"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Interrogation point in BD FACS Calibur"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Point within the fluidic subsystem at which the laser intersects the stream, illuminating the cells where they emit their fluorescence and scatter the light. The laser irradiates the cell at the interrogation point."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.flocyte.com/FRTP/Resources/flow_cytometry_glossary.htm, 2007-05-11"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:BFO_0000029 .

ns1:OBI_0400061 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "jet_in_air_flow_chamber"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "jet_in_air_flow_chamber"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Jet-in-air flow chamber in DakoCytomation MoFlo high-speed cell sorter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A flow cell in which the cells are pinched off as droplets and allowed to drop through the air. The laser intersects with the cell in mid-air. A jet in air flow chamber allows the laser to intersect with the cells without any intermittent media other than air."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.flocyte.com/FRTP/Resources/flow_cytometry_glossary.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:BFO_0000029 .

ns1:OBI_0400062 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "krypton ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "krypton ion laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Lexel 95L krypton laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A krypton-ion laser is an ion laser that uses krypton as the lasing medium. These lasers can emit at 468, 476, 482, 520, 531, 568, 647 (the most powerful line), and 676 nm all at once. They have much lower gain than argon lasers however."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "John Quinn"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400060 .

ns1:OBI_0400063 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "LactoScope C4"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "LactoScope C4"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LactoScope C4 Automatic Economical"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A LactoScope_C4 is a spectrophotometer with which the composition of milk and milk products is analysed via infrared technology. The LactoScope determines the amount of the constituents fat, protein, lactose and the total solids content with extreme accuracy."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Josef Spidlen"@en,
        "Melanie Courtot"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.aicompanies.com/DeltaCD/lacto_ftir_auto.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400115 .

ns1:OBI_0400066 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "logarithmic voltage amplifier"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "logarithmic voltage amplifier"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "HLVA-100 logarithmic voltage amplifier developed by FEMTO Messtechnik, GmbH"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A logarithmic voltage amplifier is an analog electronic circuit that puts out a voltage or current proportional to the voltage or current at its input, with logarithmic proportionality. In an analog system, the logarithmic voltage amplifier is used to present parameters with a high dynamic range on a more useful scale."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400101 .

ns1:OBI_0400067 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "long pass filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "long pass filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "750 LP filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A long pass filter is an optical filter that passes high wavelengths of light but attenuates (or reduces) wavelengths lower than the cutoff frequency. A long pass filter with a cutoff of 500 nm would pass all wavelengths greater than 500 nm."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/high-pass_filter"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400079 .

ns1:OBI_0400068 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "LSR2"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "LSR2"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A LSR2 is a sorter manufactured by Becton Dickinson. It features digital electronics, a solid state 488 nm blue laser and optionally can also have any combination of solid state UV (355 nm) and violet (405 nm) lasers and the a HeNe (633 nm) ion laser. The LSR2 has the filters and PMTs to work with 13 fluorescent parameters. The LSR II is one of the most common sorters in use."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.bdbiosciences.com/external_files/is/doc/mkt_lit/brochures/live/web_enabled/SJ-0142-00LSR2.pdf"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400069 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Luminex 100"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Luminex 100"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The Luminex 100 is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Luminex. It is a single laser system (575 nm) with avalanche photodiodes in red and infrared and a single PMT for fluorescence. The flow chamber is a square quartz cuvette."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.luminexcorp.com/products/luminex_100IS.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400070 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Luminex 200"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Luminex 200"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Luminex_200 is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Luminex. The optical specifications are: Reporter laser: 532 nm, nominal output 10 - 15 mW, maximum 500 mW, frequency-doubled diode; mode of operation, continuous wave (CW). Classification laser: 635 nm, 9.1 __ 6%, maximum output 25 mW, diode; mode of operation, continuous wave (CW) Reporter detector: Photomultiplier tube, detection bandwidth of 565 - 585 nm Classification detector and doublet discriminator: Avalanche photo diodes with temperature compensation"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.luminexcorp.com/support/faqs.html"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400071 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "MACS Quant"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "MACS Quant"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A MACS Quant is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Miltenyi. It uses digital electronics, and has three lasers of wavelengths 405 nm, 488 nm, and 635 nm. It has filters and detectors to collect 7 fluorescent parameters and 2 scatter parameters. The MACS Quant is an analyser usually used in research applications."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.miltenyi.com"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400074 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mixed argon-krypton gas laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "mixed argon-krypton gas laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "argon-krypton laser in a cytometer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A mixed argon krypton gas laser is an ion laser in which the lasing medium is a mixture of argon and krypton. A mixed argon-krypton laser can by used to irradiate cells in a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.eio.com/repairfaq/sam/laserarg.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400060 .

ns1:OBI_0400075 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "MoFlo"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "MoFlo"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "MoFlo at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A MoFlo is a flow_cytometer_sorter manufactured by Dako Cytomation. It features digital electronics, the option to include several lasers (solid state 488 nm, 635 nm, and a 351 nm diode laser), and has the filtering and collection capacity for up to 10 flouresecent parameters. The MoFlo is an instrument that can be used to both analyze quantitatively and collect cells in a flowing medium."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.dakousa.com/index/prod_search/prod_groups.htm?productareaid=16"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400077 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "neodymium-YAG laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "neodymium-YAG laser"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Neodymium-YAG Laser in DURIP99 System"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Neodymium-YAG (yttrium aluminum garnet) laser is a solid state laser in which the lasing medium is a solid rod of crystalline material pumped by a flash lamp or a diode laser. Typical output wavelengths are 355, 532, and 1064 nm. A neodymium-YAG laser can by used to irradiate cells in a flow cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "John Quinn"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400096 .

ns1:OBI_0400080 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "optical subsystem"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "optical subsystem"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "optical subsystem of a cytometer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a device or part of a device that deals with the behavior and properties of light and the interaction of light with matter. Commonly optical subsystems consist of an excitation optics and collection optics. The excitation optics of a flow cytometer optical subsystem consist of the laser and lenses that are used to shape and focus the laser beam. The collections optics consist of a collection lens to collect light emitted from the particle laser beam interaction and a system of optical mirrors and filters to route specified wavelengths of the collected light to designated optical detectors. The optical subsystem in a flow cytometer consists of the equipment used to irradiate particles, and collect the light either emitted or scattered by those particles."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "DS: Is 'subsystem' necessary or is 'optical_system' enough. Not sure its graph position since an optical subsystem is not necessarily an instrument, but more likely part of one."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person: Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "John Quinn"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000051 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400078 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000051 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400065 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000051 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400079 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0400084 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "photomultiplier tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "photomultiplier tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "R9647 by manufactured by Hamamatsu"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A photomultiplier is a device that is normally in the form of a tube, that uses a photocathode to convert photons into photoelectrons which are then amplified. PMTs are typically used to detect SSC and fluorescent parameters. Cytometers have a PMT for each color they can collect."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://cyto.mednet.ucla.edu/Protocols/flow.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000370 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000395 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000453 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000832,
        ns1:OBI_0000967 .

ns1:OBI_0400085 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "piezo electric crystal"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "piezo electric crystal"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "quartz piezoelectric crystal, topaz piezoelectric crystal, piezoelectric crystal in a sonar"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Apparatus in the fluidic subsystem of sorters that vibrates to break up the stream coming out of the flow chamber into droplets for sorting. The peizo electric crystal vibrates in a manner that breaks off droplets at regular intervals. Not all droplets contain a cell."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.flocyte.com/FRTP/Resources/flow_cytometry_glossary.htm"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000232 "think this is natural thing, not a device HP/JF"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000377 ],
        ns1:OBI_0001033 .

ns1:OBI_0400086 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "plate loader"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "plate loader"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "FC 500 plate loader"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics system. A plate loader positions the wells of a multi-well plate under the aspiration tube is a preset order. A plate loader is used for high throughput applications."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "measurement function is not corret as discussed on April 26 dev call. Will add new function such as positioning function. Add to tracker will discuss in the future."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.beckmancoulter.com/literature/Bioresearch/P-10202A.pdf"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000383 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0400087 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "preamplifier"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "preamplifier"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Built in preamplifier in a Hamamatsu H9656 PMT"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A preamplifier is part of the electronics subsystem. It converts the current output from its associated detector to a voltage. The preamplifier is the first stage in analog electronics signal processing."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400101 .

ns1:OBI_0400088 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "quartz cuvette flow chamber"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "quartz cuvette flow chamber"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "CVF-Q-10 flow chamber, CV-Q-10 flow chamber"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A flow cell in which the laser irradiates the cell as it passes through a quartz cuvette. A quartz cuvette flow chamber can be used to allow the laser to irradiate cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.flocyte.com/FRTP/Resources/flow_cytometry_glossary.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400043 .

ns1:OBI_0400089 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Reflection"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Reflection"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Reflection at TSRI Flow Cytometry Core Facility"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Reflection is a sorter manufactured by iCyte. It uses digital signal processing, and can be configured with lasers of the users choice from among these excitation wavelengths: 355, 405,488, 532, 635nm. It accommodates up to 48 traditional PMTs. Options include an acousto-optical tunable filter (AOTF) and 16 channel spectrometer (370 to 730 nm). The various detection components can be uniquely configured across multiple Highly Automated Parallel Sorting (HAPS) modules. The Reflection can be used to analyse, sort, and collect cells."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.i-cyt.com/reflection.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400099 .

ns1:OBI_0400091 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cytometer sample tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "cytometer sample tube"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "sample tube in a cytometer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A particle delivery vessel. The cytometer sample tube is a vessel in which the sample is introduced to the cytometer. Frequently the tube is placed on the cytometer in such a manner that a seal is formed between the tube and cytometer, and gas is used to create enough pressure to push the sample out of the tube and into the cytometer."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0000836 .

ns1:OBI_0400094 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "sheath tank"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "sheath tank"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 sheath tank"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics system. The sheath tank is the vessel that holds the sheath fluid at a constant pressure, allowing for it to be pushed into the flow chamber at a constant rate. The sheath tank holds the pressurized sheath fluid."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000401 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000370 ],
        ns1:OBI_0002089 .

ns1:OBI_0400095 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "short pass filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "short pass filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "620 SP filter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A short pass filter is an optical filter that passes low wavelengths of light but attenuates (or reduces) wavelengths higher than the cutoff frequency. A short pass filter with a cutoff of 500 nm would pass all wavelengths less than 500 nm."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Low-pass_filter"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400079 .

ns1:OBI_0400097 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Somacount"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "Somacount"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A Somacount is a flow_cytometer_analyser manufactured by Bently Instruments. It is a specialized tool for counting somatic cells in milk by specifically staining them with Ethidium Bromide and counting the cells that fluoresce. It has one laser, and the filters and a PMT for the single parameter. There are three sizes available, the 150, 300, and 500 with the number indicating the maximum number of cells that can be analysed per hour. The Somacount is an example of a very specific use cytometer; it exclusively counts somatic cells in milk."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.bentleyinstruments.com/somacount.html#Anchor-Bentley-49575"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400098 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SomaScope"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "SomaScope"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "SomaScope Mark II Automatic Economical"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The SomaScope is an instrument to quantify somatic cells in milk."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Josef Spidlen"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "\"http://www.aicompanies.com/DeltaCD/soma_auto_adv.htm, 2007-05-10\""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400008 .

ns1:OBI_0400100 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "syringe pump"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "syringe pump"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "NE-1000 Single Syringe Pump"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics system. A syringe pump can be used to inject the sample fluid and cells into the sheath fluid in the flow chamber. Syringe pumps are useful for creating stable flow rates."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.answers.com/topic/syringe, 2007-05-11"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000370 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000383 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000967 .

ns1:OBI_0400102 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "waste tank"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "waste tank"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "LSR2 waste tank"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Part of the fluidics systems. In analyzers the sheath and sample fluid, once analyzed is dumped into a waste tank. The waste tank is where the fluids passing through the cytometer end up after the analysis is finished."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person:John Quinn"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Practical Flow Cytometry 4th Edition, Howard Shapiro, ISBN-10: 0471411256, ISBN-13: 978-0471411253"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000370 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000967 .

ns1:OBI_0400104 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "array scanner"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "array scanner"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "GenePix 4200A, GenePix4000B"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "An processed material which acquires images of fluorescence (induced with lasers) from labeled molecules on the surface of the microarray chip"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: MGED Ontology"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000397 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000453 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000398 .

ns1:OBI_0400105 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "arrayer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "arrayer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "BioRobotics Microgrid II TAS, Affymetrix GMS 417"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a device which deposits biological material onto a substrate in a defined pattern."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "MO_697 arrayer"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000383 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0400108 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "heating block"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "heating block"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "An instrument used to heat and/or maintain material at a set temperature."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A heating block is an instrument or part of an instrument which raises or maintains the temperature of a sample to a defined constant temperature during certain parts of an assay"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "MO"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000371 ],
        ns1:OBI_0001034 .

ns1:OBI_0400109 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "homogenizer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "homogenizer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "mortar, blender"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A homogenizer is an instrument for the homogenization of various types of material, such as tissue, plant, food, soil, and many others."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot"@en,
        "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homogenizer"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000377 ],
        ns1:OBI_0001033 .

ns1:OBI_0400111 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hybridization station"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "hybridization station"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Labnet Problot12"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A device which is used to maintain the temperature of one or more hybridization_chamber(s) at a defined, constant temperature."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "MO_497 hybridization station"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0002089 ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( ns1:OBI_0000968 [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000051 ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0400110 ] [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000401 ] ) ] .

ns1:OBI_0400117 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "vacuum dryer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "vacuum dryer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Model 777 Microarray Oven"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "An instrument which removes liquid by the application of negative pressure,  i.e. vacuum."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "MO"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000370 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000383 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000401 ],
        ns1:OBI_0002089 .

ns1:OBI_0400118 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "vortexer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "vortexer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "VWR  Genie 2"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A vortexer is an instrument that mixes small vials of liquid by creating a rotation of the liquid around its own center. It consists of an electric motor with the drive shaft oriented vertically and attached to a cupped rubber piece mounted slightly off-center. As the motor runs the rubber piece oscillates rapidly in a circular motion. When a test tube or other appropriate container is pressed into the rubber cup (or touched to its edge) the motion is transmitted to the liquid inside and a vortex is created."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot"@en,
        "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "vortex_mixer"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vortex_mixer"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000377 ],
        ns1:OBI_0001033 .

ns1:OBI_0400119 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "microarray wash station"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "microarray wash station"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "ArrayIt(r) Microarray Wash Station"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a device that is used to wash Affymetrix-type arrays."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "MO_626 wash_station"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000401 ],
        ns1:OBI_0002089 .

ns1:OBI_0400121 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "molecular crosslinker"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "molecular crosslinker"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Stratalinker"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a device that is able to chemically join two or more molecules."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "AL: if we intend that other ontologies can be used in conjunction with OBI, we shouldn't have such a general term used specifically for chemically joining two or more molecules. I'm sure there are other \"crosslinkers\" that are on a much different scale in engineering etc. I have moved the original label to be an alternative term, and have renamed the main label accordingly."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "molecular crosslinker"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "MO ?? cannot be found in MO"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000401 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000367 ],
        ns1:OBI_0001032,
        ns1:OBI_0002089 .

ns1:OBI_0400155 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "water bath"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "water bath"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "A water bath was used to allow for cell incubation at 38 degree centigrade for 8 hours."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A water bath is a temperature control bath in which a water acts as contact medium enabling temperature transfer from the heating element or cooling element to the sample. The temperature can be controlled in the 0 to 100 degree centigrade range (under normal pressure)."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "PERSON: Daniel Schober"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400120 .

ns1:OBI_0400157 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "oil bath"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "oil bath"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "An oil bath was used to allow for fast reaction of two chemical compounds during a 2 hour period."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "An oil bath is a temperature control bath in which oil acts as contact medium for the temperature transfer (from heating or cooling elements to the sample)."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "PERSON: Daniel Schober"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0400120 .

ns1:OBI_0400158 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "digital-to-analog converter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "digital-to-analog converter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "A digital-to-analog_converter is used to convert a computergenerated discrete signal into a continuous analog one, e.g. a sound."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A digital-to-analog_converter is an instrument that converts a finite resolution digital signal into an infinite resolution analog signal."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "PERSON: Daniel Schober"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000393 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0400170 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "microscope slide"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "microscope slide"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 9668975.Microscope slide for enhanced analysis of DNA damage using the comet assay."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "a microscope slide is a device usually made of glass which is used as a solid matrix for (biological) material deposited on its surface and which is compatible for use with a microscope instrument"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Phillippe Rocca-Serra"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI biomaterial branch"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000085 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000399 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000968 .

ns1:OBI_0500004 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "n-to-1 design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "n-to-1 design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000125 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "N-of-1 design is a cross-over design in which the same patient is repeatedly randomised to receive either the experimental treatment or its control (Senn, 1993)."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Adapted from  http://www.childrens-mercy.org/stats/definitions/crossover.htm and source:http://symptomresearch.nih.gov/chapter_6/sec1/csss1pg1.htm)"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0500003 .

ns1:OBI_0500005 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "matched pairs design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "matched pairs design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 17288613-BSTRACT: BACKGROUND: Physicians in Canadian emergency departments (EDs) annually treat 185,000 alert and stable trauma victims who are at risk for cervical spine (C-spine) injury. However, only 0.9% of these patients have suffered a cervical spine fracture. Current use of radiography is not efficient. The Canadian C-Spine Rule is designed to allow physicians to be more selective and accurate in ordering C-spine radiography, and to rapidly clear the C-spine without the need for radiography in many patients. The goal of this phase III study is to evaluate the effectiveness of an active strategy to implement the Canadian C-Spine Rule into physician practice. Specific objectives are to: 1) determine clinical impact, 2) determine sustainability, 3) evaluate performance, and 4) conduct an economic evaluation. METHODS: We propose a matched-pair cluster design study that compares outcomes during three consecutive 12-months before, after, and decay periods at six pairs of intervention and control sites. These 12 hospital ED sites will be stratified as teaching or community hospitals, matched according to baseline C-spine radiography ordering rates, and then allocated within each pair to either intervention or control groups. During the after period at the intervention sites, simple and inexpensive strategies will be employed to actively implement the Canadian C-Spine Rule. The following outcomes will be assessed: 1) measures of clinical impact, 2) performance of the Canadian C-Spine Rule, and 3) economic measures. During the 12-month decay period, implementation strategies will continue, allowing us to evaluate the sustainability of the effect. We estimate a sample size of 4,800 patients in each period in order to have adequate power to evaluate the main outcomes. DISCUSSION: Phase I successfully derived the Canadian C-Spine Rule and phase II confirmed the accuracy and safety of the rule, hence, the potential for physicians to improve care. What remains unknown is the actual change in clinical behaviors that can be affected by implementation of the Canadian C-Spine Rule, and whether implementation can be achieved with simple and inexpensive measures. We believe that the Canadian C-Spine Rule has the potential to significantly reduce health care costs and improve the efficiency of patient flow in busy Canadian EDs."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000125 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A matched pair design is a study design which use groups of individuals associated (hence matched) to each other based on a set of criteria, one member going to one treatment, the other member receiving the other treatment."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.holah.karoo.net/experimentaldesigns.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0500000 .

ns1:OBI_0500006 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "parallel group design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "parallel group design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 17408389-Purpose: Proliferative vitreoretinopathy (PVR) is the most important reason for blindness following retinal detachment. Presently, vitreous tamponades such as gas or silicone oil cannot contact the lower part of the retina. A heavier-than-water tamponade displaces the inflammatory and PVR-stimulating environment from the inferior area of the retina. The Heavy Silicone Oil versus Standard Silicone Oil Study (HSO Study) is designed to answer the question of whether a heavier-than-water tamponade improves the prognosis of eyes with PVR of the lower retina. Methods: The HSO Study is a multicentre, randomized, prospective controlled clinical trial comparing two endotamponades within a two-arm parallel group design. Patients with inferiorly and posteriorly located PVR are randomized to either heavy silicone oil or standard silicone oil as a tamponading agent. Three hundred and fifty consecutive patients are recruited per group. After intraoperative re-attachment, patients are randomized to either standard silicone oil (1000 cSt or 5000 cSt) or Densiron((R)) as a tamponading agent. The main endpoint criteria are complete retinal attachment at 12 months and change of visual acuity (VA) 12 months postoperatively compared with the preoperative VA. Secondary endpoints include complete retinal attachment before endotamponade removal, quality of life analysis and the number of retina affecting re-operation within 1 year of follow-up. Results: The design and early recruitment phase of the study are described. Conclusions: The results of this study will uncover whether or not heavy silicone oil improves the prognosis of eyes with PVR."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000125 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A parallel group design or independent measure design is a study design which uses unique experimental unit each experimental group, in other word no two individuals are shared between experimental groups, hence also known as parallel group design. Subjects of a treatment group receive a unique combination of independent variable values making up a treatment"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "independent measure design"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "http://www.holah.karoo.net/experimentaldesigns.htm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OBI_0500000 .

ns1:OBI_0500008 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "balanced incomplete block design"@en ;
