    ns1:IAO_0000115 "High molecular weight, linear polymers, composed of nucleotides containing ribose and linked by phosphodiester bonds; RNA is central to the synthesis of proteins."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000412 ns1:chebi.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:CHEBI_33696 .

ns1:IAO_0000300 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "textual entity"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "textual entity"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "Words, sentences, paragraphs, and the written (non-figure) parts of publications are all textual entities"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A textual entity is a part of a manifestation (FRBR sense), a generically dependent continuant whose concretizations are patterns of glyphs intended to be interpreted as words, formulas, etc."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "AR, (IAO call 2009-09-01): a document as a whole is not typically a textual entity, because it has pictures in it - rather there are parts of it that are textual entities. Examples: The title, paragraph 2 sentence 7, etc."@en,
        "MC, 2009-09-14 (following IAO call 2009-09-01): textual entities live at the FRBR (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_Requirements_for_Bibliographic_Records) manifestation level. Everything is significant: line break, pdf and html versions of same document are different textual entities."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "text"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns1:IAO_0000030 .

ns1:OBI_0001051 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "DNA extract"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "DNA extract"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "The output of an extraction process in which DNA molecules are purified in order to exclude DNA from organellas."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jie Zheng"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "Group: UPenn group"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000643 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:CHEBI_16991 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000257 ],
        ns1:OBI_0001010 .

ns1:OBI_0100060 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cultured cell population"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "cultured cell population"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "A cultured cell population applied in an experiment: \"293 cells expressing TrkA were serum-starved for 18 hours and then neurotrophins were added for 10 min before cell harvest.\"  (Lee, Ramee, et al. \"Regulation of cell survival by secreted proneurotrophins.\" Science 294.5548 (2001): 1945-1948).\\n\\nA cultured cell population maintained in vitro: \"Rat cortical neurons from 15 day embryos are grown in dissociated cell culture and maintained in vitro for 8–12 weeks\" (Dichter, Marc A. \"Rat cortical neurons in cell culture: culture methods, cell morphology, electrophysiology, and synapse formation.\" Brain Research 149.2 (1978): 279-293)." ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A processed material comprised of a collection of cultured cells that has been continuously maintained together in culture and shares a common propagation history."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "2013-6-5 MHB: This OBI class was formerly called 'cell culture', but label changed and definition updated following CLO alignment efforts in spring 2013, during which the intent of this class was clarified to refer to portions of a culture or line rather than a complete cell culture or line."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Matthew Brush"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000118 "cell culture sample" ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "PERSON:Matthew Brush"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "The extent of a 'cultured cell population' is restricted only in that all cell members must share a propagation history (ie be derived through a common lineage of passages from an initial culture). In being defined in this way, this class can be used to refer to the populations that researchers actually use in the practice of science - ie are the inputs to culturing, experimentation, and sharing. The cells in such populations will be a relatively uniform population as they have experienced similar selective pressures due to their continuous co-propagation. And this population will also have a single passage number, again owing to their common passaging history. Cultured cell populations represent only a collection of cells (ie do not include media, culture dishes, etc), and include populations of cultured unicellular organisms or cultured multicellular organism cells. They can exist under active culture, stored in a quiescent state for future use, or applied experimentally."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom ns1:CL_0000010 ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000643 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000312 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0600024 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:OBI_0000643 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:CL_0000010 ],
        ns1:OBI_0000047 .

ns1:IAO_0000314 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "document part"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "document part"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "An abstract, introduction, method or results section."@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "an information content entity that is part of a document"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ns1:IAO_0000310 ],
        ns1:IAO_0000030 .

ns1:OBI_0000571 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "manufacturer role"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "manufacturer role"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000112 "With respect to The Accuri C6 Flow Cytometer System, the organization Accuri bears the role manufacturer role.  With respect to a transformed line of tissue culture cells derived by a specific lab, the lab whose personnel isolated the cll line bears the role manufacturer role.  With respect to a specific antibody produced by an individual scientist, the scientist who purifies, characterizes and distributes the anitbody bears the role manufacturer role."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000123 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "Manufacturer role is a role which inheres in a person or organization and which is realized by a manufacturing process."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "GROUP:  Role Branch"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "OBI"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0000052 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom [ a owl:Class ;
                    owl:unionOf ( ns1:NCBITaxon_9606 ns1:OBI_0000245 ) ] ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom ns1:OBI_0000457 ;
            owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000054 ],
        ns1:BFO_0000023 .

ns1:OBI_0000643 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has grain"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000111 "has grain"^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000114 ns1:IAO_0000120 ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "the relation of the cells in the finger of the skin to the finger, in which an indeterminate number of grains are parts of the whole by virtue of being grains in a collective that is part of the whole, and in which removing one granular part does not nec- essarily damage or diminish the whole. Ontological Whether there is a fixed, or nearly fixed number of parts - e.g. fingers of the hand, chambers of the heart, or wheels of a car - such that there can be a notion of a single one being missing, or whether, by contrast, the number of parts is indeterminate - e.g., cells in the skin of the hand, red cells in blood, or rubber molecules in the tread of the tire of the wheel of the car."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:IAO_0000116 "Discussion in Karslruhe with, among others, Alan Rector, Stefan Schulz, Marijke Keet, Melanie Courtot, and Alan Ruttenberg. Definition take from the definition of granular parthood in the cited paper. Needs work to put into standard form"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en ;
    ns1:IAO_0000119 "PAPER: Granularity, scale and collectivity: When size does and does not matter, Alan Rector, Jeremy Rogers, Thomas Bittner, Journal of Biomedical Informatics 39 (2006) 333-349"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf ns1:BFO_0000051 .

